  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Utah total $5.5B for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $4.2B, making DOD the dominant buyer in the state. Award activity reached 8,340 contracts with an average award size of $659K, and obligations are up 5.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows variability: FY21 was $4B, FY22 was $5.3B, FY23 was $6.3B, FY24 was $7.2B, and FY25 was $5.2B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $2.9B. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP is the largest vendor by obligations at $2.9B, followed by ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $482M and L3 TECHNOLOGIES, INC. at $277M. Other notable industries include Nonferrous Metal (except Copper and Aluminum) Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding at $483M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $240M. This picture shows concentration by buyer, vendor, and industry in the current fiscal-year-to-date totals, keeping in mind current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the concentration of buying power in Utah?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $4.2B, concentrating a large share of the state’s federal spending. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $2.9B, matching the largest vendor, NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP at $2.9B, which aligns industry demand and prime contractor presence. Other agencies contribute smaller shares, including the Department of the Treasury at $510M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $266M. This buyer and industry mix shapes where obligations flow within Utah."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate federal obligations in Utah?",
        "body": "NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP leads vendors with $2.9B in obligations. ASAHI REFINING USA INC follows with $482M and L3 TECHNOLOGIES, INC. follows with $277M. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry at $2.9B, supported by Nonferrous Metal (except Copper and Aluminum) Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding at $483M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $240M."
      }
    ]
  },
